{"term":"eccentric","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ab3733b87d97e79b43","definition":"Not at or in the centre; away from the centre.","example":"Suppose the small pulley on the right to be the driver, the larger wheel with an internal rack and the eccentric wheel within will be driven in opposite directions by the bands represented in the cut, while at the same time motion will be imparted to the intermediate pinion on the left, both round its own centre, and also round the common centre of the circular rack and concentric wheel.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["eccentrical","excentrical"],"antonyms":["consistent","conventional","mainstream","normal","ordinary","uneccentric"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["eccentric abstraction","eccentrically","eccentric anomaly","eccentricate","eccentric contraction","eccentric flint","eccentric hypertrophy","eccentric kangaroo unicycle","eccentrize","isoeccentric","photoeccentric","uneccentric"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eccentric#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b2b416e5a423cf67f7","definition":"Not perfectly circular; elliptical.","example":"As of 2008, Margaret had the most eccentric orbit of any moon in the solar system, though Nereid's mean eccentricity is greater.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["eccentrical","excentrical"],"antonyms":["consistent","conventional","mainstream","normal","ordinary","uneccentric"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["eccentric abstraction","eccentrically","eccentric anomaly","eccentricate","eccentric contraction","eccentric flint","eccentric hypertrophy","eccentric kangaroo unicycle","eccentrize","isoeccentric","photoeccentric","uneccentric"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eccentric#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:90f0ea80c83b772b9a","definition":"Having a different center; not concentric.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["eccentrical","excentrical"],"antonyms":["consistent","conventional","mainstream","normal","ordinary","uneccentric"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["eccentric abstraction","eccentrically","eccentric anomaly","eccentricate","eccentric contraction","eccentric flint","eccentric hypertrophy","eccentric kangaroo unicycle","eccentrize","isoeccentric","photoeccentric","uneccentric"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eccentric#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:65d6c5b6091dc81e82","definition":"Of a person, deviating from the norm; behaving unexpectedly or differently; unconventional and slightly strange.","example":"1801, Author not named, Fyfield (John), entry in Eccentric Biography; Or, Sketches of Remarkable Characters, Ancient and Modern, page 127,\nHe was a man of a most eccentric turn of mind, and great singularity of conduct.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["eccentrical","excentrical","odd","abnormal"],"antonyms":["consistent","conventional","mainstream","normal","ordinary","uneccentric"],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["eccentric abstraction","eccentrically","eccentric anomaly","eccentricate","eccentric contraction","eccentric flint","eccentric hypertrophy","eccentric kangaroo unicycle","eccentrize","isoeccentric","photoeccentric","uneccentric"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eccentric#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e7f296601b490f04ac","definition":"Of a motion, against or in the opposite direction of contraction of a muscle (such as results from flexion of the lower arm (bending of the elbow joint) by an external force while contracting the triceps and othe