m to drive the engine backwards. To be able, therefore, to reverse the motion of the engine, it would only be necessary to be able to reverse the position of the eccentrics, which may be accomplished by either of two expedients.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["nonconformist","crank","odd duck","weirdo"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["eccentric abstraction","eccentrically","eccentric anomaly","eccentricate","eccentric contraction","eccentric flint","eccentric hypertrophy","eccentric kangaroo unicycle","eccentrize","isoeccentric","photoeccentric","uneccentric","acentric"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eccentric#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:61e71d40e10913780e","definition":"An exercise that goes against or in the opposite direction of contraction of a muscle.","example":"Research tells us that eccentrics, heavy partials, and static exercise may require several days or weeks of recovery time.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["nonconformist","crank","odd duck","weirdo"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["eccentric abstraction","eccentrically","eccentric anomaly","eccentricate","eccentric contraction","eccentric flint","eccentric hypertrophy","eccentric kangaroo unicycle","eccentrize","isoeccentric","photoeccentric","uneccentric","acentric"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eccentric#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɪkˈsɛntɹɪk/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/30/En-au-eccentric.ogg/En-au-eccentric.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["eccentric abstraction","eccentrically","eccentric anomaly","eccentricate","eccentric contraction","eccentric flint","eccentric hypertrophy","eccentric kangaroo unicycle","eccentrize","isoeccentric","p